            <ArticleTitle>Studies in copper status and atherosclerosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1186-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Findings of this paper indicate that leucocyte copper has a significant link with the level of atherosclerosis found within the groups studied. Therefore copper may be involved in the mechanisms associated with ischaemic heart disease (IHD).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
